<title>INDIA: India Glaxo 1996 net higher.</title>
<headline>India Glaxo 1996 net higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		479.0     vs    1,850.9</p>
<p>    Net sales	     6,450.1     vs    8,415.6</p>
<p>    Gross sales	   6,999.5     vs    9,071.4</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	   4.0     vs	  2.9</p>
<p>    Other income	    314.8     vs	594.5</p>
<p>    Expenditure	   5,727.0     vs    7,783.0</p>
<p>    Interest costs	   87.3     vs	143.5</p>
<p>    Depreciation	    120.1     vs	181.0</p>
<p>    Tax			 351.5     vs	787.5</p>
<p>Profit on sale of</p>
<p>    Family Prods unit	 --	vs    1,735.8</p>
<p>Note: Glaxo India Ltd is a subsidiary of the U.K.-based Glaxo Wellcome plc. Glaxo said the year-ago figures were for the 18 months from July 1994 to December 1995. The previous years' dividend excludes a special dividend of 17.5 rupees per share.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom (91-22-265 9000)</p>
</text>
